{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 200,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is out there like a massive apartment\ncomplex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3133,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just 20 minutes away\nby subway from Vienna City center."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7500,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, tenants\npay around 600 to €800 a month"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12066,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a spacious two bedroom apartment,\ncomplete with onsite"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15866,
    "dDurationMs": 5134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "daycare, underground\nparking, green spaces and rooftop pools."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21366,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly placed decked out\napartments in New York are listed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25166,
    "dDurationMs": 4334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for almost 4,000 USD per month."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29933,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Amsterdam,\nthe minimum is about 2000 per month,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33900,
    "dDurationMs": 3766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but 3000 is more common."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37800,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, in London, 2,500 pounds\nseems like the bare minimum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42700,
    "dDurationMs": 400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43100,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in London, in New York, people earn\nsignificantly more money than in Vienna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47466,
    "dDurationMs": 2734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if we account for that extra income,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can see that Vienna still appears to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53366,
    "dDurationMs": 6167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an exceptionally affordable capital city\nwhere renters spend about 30%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59533,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of their salary on rent, compared to 70"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62533,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 80% in London and New York."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66333,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That massive cost of living gap\nis the primary reason why The Economist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69900,
    "dDurationMs": 6066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consistently ranks Vienna as the most or\nsecond most livable major city on Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76100,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how did Vienna solve the housing\naffordability crisis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79566,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is still plaguing\nevery other global city on the planet?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84000,
    "dDurationMs": 1733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On paper, the answer looks simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85733,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna's government has simply built a lot\na lot of public housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90533,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But upon closer inspection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91900,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Vienna Solution seemed way\nmore radical than that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95833,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see here, arguably\nthe concept of a free rental market"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100033,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't exist in Vienna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101633,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, 31% of renters live in city"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104800,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "controlled homes, 26% live in nonprofit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109166,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "controlled homes, and then finally 33%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112466,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "live in rent controlled private homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115466,
    "dDurationMs": 5834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's really only 10% of Vienna's\nrenters that pay a market determined rent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121366,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So is the answer to the global\nhousing crisis that this, like London"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125066,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and New York, had just turn to basically\nhousing socialism like in Vienna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131300,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps, although we have discovered\nthat below the surface,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134666,
    "dDurationMs": 634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna's rental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135300,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "market is a little less perfect\nthan it seems, and that there are three"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139266,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unique problems holding back cities\nfrom copying Vienna's approach."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143566,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to understand this, we first need\nto understand how public housing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146933,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "took over Vienna,\nas this fascinating graph"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150000,
    "dDurationMs": 4166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by University of Vienna researchers\nJustin Carey and Walter Madsen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154166,
    "dDurationMs": 5934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that shows Vienna's massive public housing\nproject, shown in red and yellow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160233,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "started with a big surge in 1922"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164000,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then really exploded after 1950."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167700,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what can explain these\ntwo massive shifts?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171033,
    "dDurationMs": 2333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, we need to keep in mind\nthat Vienna, for the longest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173366,
    "dDurationMs": 4834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time, used to be the majestic capital\nof the Austro-Hungarian Empire,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178600,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which fell apart after the First World\nWar, which ended in 1918."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182700,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In these circumstances, Austria's economy,\nof course collapsed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186466,
    "dDurationMs": 1667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "causing hyperinflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188133,
    "dDurationMs": 5467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as prices everywhere skyrocketed,\nstrict rent controls prevented landlords"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193600,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from raising the rent,\nmeaning that rental properties essentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197100,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "became worthless overnight\nand therefore, while returning soldiers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201500,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needed new homes in Vienna,\nprivate landlords refused to build them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206033,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "preferring\nto keep their land vacant instead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209800,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when, in May 1919,\nthe Social democratic Workers Party"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213866,
    "dDurationMs": 4234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "won an absolute majority in the city's\nfirst fully democratic election,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218366,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they recognized a clear economic reality\nand the strict rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223133,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "private capital would never return\nto build affordable homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227166,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, most economists\nwould therefore probably recommend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230333,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to abolish rent controls\nto incentivize people to build more homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235133,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is where Vienna's story deviates\nfrom most other cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239500,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This period came to be known\nas red Vienna for a reason."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243366,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see,\nif the private sector would not build,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245666,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the state would just have to step in\nand do it themselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249300,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, this was easier\nsaid than done."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252366,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna was in deep financial trouble,\nso how were they ever going to be able"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256766,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to find the money to buy all that\nprivate land and build homes on them?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260866,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Based on the history of Vienna, we have\nidentified the following three steps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265200,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first step was the so-called body\npolitic that heavily taxed vacant land."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270900,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, what would you do\nif hyperinflation had pushed up oil"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274066,
    "dDurationMs": 3434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prices, but rent controls\nprevented you from raising your prices?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277833,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now, on top of that,\nyou had to pay a tax if you left your land"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281866,
    "dDurationMs": 1067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "vacant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282933,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For many Viennese landowners,\nthe answer was clear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287100,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was no other option\nthan to sell vacant land to the city"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290533,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at rock bottom prices, often\n10 to 15% of peacetime values."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295433,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1914, and once cheap land was secured,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299433,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna needed to find the money\nto build the new houses on this land."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303500,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So City Councilor\nHugo Breitner introduced two new taxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308100,
    "dDurationMs": 5066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first one a residential construction\ntax known as von bath Toya, was levied"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313166,
    "dDurationMs": 4234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "progressively on the construction\nof larger, mainly private housing units,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317566,
    "dDurationMs": 4334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the second one, a luxury tax,\nwas levied primarily on luxury"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321900,
    "dDurationMs": 4466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goods and services such as cars,\nhotel rooms and leisure activities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326933,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to all to fund these public homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329433,
    "dDurationMs": 4633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And with this money and the cheap\nland combined, the city was able to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334066,
    "dDurationMs": 4634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relatively quickly build about 60,000\nstate owned, high quality apartments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338733,
    "dDurationMs": 5267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "known as Gapminder Boughton housing around\n11% of the city's population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344266,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Between 1923 and 1934."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347733,
    "dDurationMs": 2567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then something strange happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350300,
    "dDurationMs": 1866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It all stagnated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352166,
    "dDurationMs": 967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what went wrong?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353133,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in 1934, Red Vienna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356100,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "abruptly ended when the conservative\nAustrian Chancellor Engelbert Dollfuss"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360800,
    "dDurationMs": 5466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "became dictator and ousted Vienna\nSocial Democrats after a brief civil war,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366733,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then after the Second World War,\nwhen democracy was restored,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370433,
    "dDurationMs": 5533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the social Democrats got back into power,\nand then they soon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375966,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reinstated their old policy of building\nlots of new social homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381000,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as you can see here,\nnot only did they build more homes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384900,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the private landlords\nreally sold a lot of their homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389500,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's because the Social Democrats\nessentially made it, again,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very difficult for them to make a profit\nthrough very strict rent controls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398833,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, together with the fact\nthat Vienna's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401433,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "historical center had been bombed,\nwhere a lot of these houses were."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405500,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There was now a super strong incentive\nfor private landlords"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408700,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to either sell to the city\nor turn their properties into offices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413133,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is why, on the one hand,\nthe number of houses rented from private"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417100,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "owners decreased after the Second World\nWar, while on the other hand,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420633,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the number of social housing in red\nand yellow boomed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 425100,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where the yellow represents\nhousing constructed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427900,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by government\nfunded cooperatives and nonprofits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431966,
    "dDurationMs": 3134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's actually these entities\nthat ended up being responsible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435100,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for massive, upscale projects\nlike Alt allowed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438833,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only this full historical picture of very,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442366,
    "dDurationMs": 4467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very aggressive state intervention\nin the real estate market can explain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446833,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why The New York Times\nreferred to Vienna as a renter's utopia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452133,
    "dDurationMs": 1567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is that actually true?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453700,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is Vienna actually a renter's Paradise?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456833,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457433,
    "dDurationMs": 5667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we get back to this graph, we can again\nsee that roughly 31% of renters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463100,
    "dDurationMs": 4266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "live in city homes, 26% in nonprofits,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467700,
    "dDurationMs": 4266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 33% of renters are under\nvery strict rent controls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472333,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then there's only 10% left\nin this so-called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476466,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "free market\nwhere landlords set the price freely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480600,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, standard economics\nwould tell us that in a fully socialized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484433,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and controlled housing market,\nthere would be massive problems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488500,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such as massive waiting lists for cheap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491533,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "housing and a big difference\nbetween a lucky in-group"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 495700,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and an unlucky group of renters\nthat has to rent on the private market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501300,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that also what the Viennese\nhousing market looks like?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504233,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, if we look at rent differences,\nwe can clearly see that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508800,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the very lucky people\nwho are in municipal housing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512366,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or in these nonprofit\ndevelopments do pay a lot less"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517300,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per square meters than those in private,\nrent controlled apartments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522033,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and especially then those in uncontrolled\nprivate apartments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526566,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They pay about 12 to €13\nper square meters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530933,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas those in municipal housing pay\nalmost half of that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535833,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Vienna's\nrental market is not very fair."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539400,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just as with rent controls\nin other cities, Vienna's model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542700,
    "dDurationMs": 4166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does create a so-called in versus out\nrental market,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546866,
    "dDurationMs": 4567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where a lucky group can live inside cheap\nhousing units, while an unlucky group"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gets to pay high prices\non the private market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554700,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as you can imagine, this can generate\nweird, unfair situations where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558900,
    "dDurationMs": 4833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high income lawyers and doctors\nand social housing pay almost half of what"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563733,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a working class immigrant family\npays in the private sector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567500,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And not surprisingly, it's apparently\nalso quite common in Vienna that outgoing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571133,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "renters demand large sums of money\nfrom new renters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574433,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to introduce them to the landlord."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577366,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is definitely not a renters\nutopia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580666,
    "dDurationMs": 2667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not a perfect housing market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583333,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, a lot of these problems\nalso exist in cities with some public"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587333,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "housing and rent controls\nlike London, New York and Amsterdam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591200,
    "dDurationMs": 1733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And actually,\neven though Vienna's uncontrolled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592933,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rents are almost twice\nas high as the cheapest municipal houses,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596733,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are still lower than rents\nin other big cities,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600300,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "indicating\nthat while there are waitlists in Vienna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603100,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "absolutely on which there is no data,\nsadly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606300,
    "dDurationMs": 5333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are probably not much longer\nthan in other big cities like Amsterdam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611866,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what's Vienna's secret?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614766,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I don't think it's the fact that there is\na lot of public housing on its own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619500,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, cities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Amsterdam and London\nalso have quite a lot of public housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625633,
    "dDurationMs": 5033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, I think the real reason why Vienna\nhas managed to stay relatively affordable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631333,
    "dDurationMs": 3167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though its population has been rising\nrecently,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is because it can actually build\nmore homes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638400,
    "dDurationMs": 3966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example, not including additions\nto existing buildings."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642666,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to Statistics Austria, 16,000\nnew units"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646266,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were built in Vienna in 2021 alone\nand in all of Austria,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650133,
    "dDurationMs": 5067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where 9 million people live, 71,000\nnew housing units were added."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655433,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's pretty substantial\nfor such a controlled market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658833,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For comparison, Los Angeles adds\nhousing units at less than half the rate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664200,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "despite having more people\nthan the entire country of Austria."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668033,
    "dDurationMs": 5433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the Vienna model is, yes, a largely\ncontrolled and socialized housing market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673833,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because the city of Vienna\nand its nonprofits actually build enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677700,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "homes, Vienna actually even has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680966,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fairly reasonable rents\nin the private sector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684266,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because only 10% of renters in Vienna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687866,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rent in the uncontrolled private sector,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690666,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the typical unfair in-out market dynamics\nthat you see in other cities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696133,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "does not affect as many people in Vienna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699333,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while far from perfect, Vienna's model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 703000,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually looks a lot better than the model\nof most other global cities."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708166,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So should all cities adopt Vienna's model\nof public housing over private housing?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713000,
    "dDurationMs": 5033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is a form of democratic socialism superior\nwhen it comes to housing?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718266,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, can Vienna's housing model\nsolve the global housing crisis?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723066,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, on the one hand,\nI think that Vienna teaches us that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727100,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you only look at the rental market\non the spectrum of rent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732000,
    "dDurationMs": 4566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "controls, more control or less control,\nthen you get it wrong."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736800,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You have cities like London and New York,\nwhere there are rent controls"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741700,
    "dDurationMs": 2733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and where there is public housing,\nwhere there's a lot of control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744433,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you have cities like Vienna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746833,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what really distinguishes them\nis that Vienna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750666,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually builds homes,\nwhereas these other cities do not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755000,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not about having rent control\nor no rent control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758933,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's about having rent control\nand public housing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763566,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and actually building more homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766533,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But sadly, there are three big problems\nthat prevent global cities"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771233,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like New York and London\nfrom copying Vienna's model 1 to 1."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775966,
    "dDurationMs": 2834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the first is that Vienna's unique\ndecline story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is when Vienna's government\ndid build a lot of new homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782066,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It did so against a backdrop\nof a shrinking population,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786600,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a shrinking population means lower demand\nand less pressure on prices."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790866,
    "dDurationMs": 2734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in this situation,\nit was possible for the city government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pretty much screw over\nprivate construction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796600,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and replace it with social housing\nwithout facing severe bottlenecks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801733,
    "dDurationMs": 467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802200,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Vienna,\nthe population is now also rising."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805533,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if we look at prices\nin the private rental market,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809866,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it really looks like so far\nthe Viennese government has actually been"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814233,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "able to keep up with construction\nbetter than private construction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819166,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in other major cities, where construction\nis actually at all time lows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824266,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, the Venice government\nnow has a century"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827900,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of experience of building homes at scale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832166,
    "dDurationMs": 3267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Other major cities\nsimply do not have these"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835433,
    "dDurationMs": 4833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sophisticated institutions\nto build public housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840266,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a good quality\nand build it quickly enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844333,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then, of course, there's more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845666,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The second major problem\nin trying to copy paste a Vienna model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849333,
    "dDurationMs": 4933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that a massive social housing program\nis, of course, very expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854533,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna is exceptional\nbecause it bought its land"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857300,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cheap during an economic collapse\na century ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861100,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Assembling that much land\nin any other city today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864600,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be incredibly expensive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867900,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "requiring major tax hikes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870900,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, the third major problem\nis about the politics of fairness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875600,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna social housing\nhas so much political support"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878300,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it targets the middle class\nrather than the poor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882933,
    "dDurationMs": 2433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is not very fair, of course."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885366,
    "dDurationMs": 4334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Social housing programs like those\nin the US or the French banlieues"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890166,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have often felt much more fair,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894133,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but ended up making inequality worse\nas it cost poverty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897866,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to concentrate\nin these large social housing projects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901166,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And these high profile failures\nhelped reduce"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904200,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the political support\nfor all social housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908033,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, my main takeaway\nfrom how Vienna solve the housing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911866,
    "dDurationMs": 5467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "affordability crisis is that you shouldn't\njust talk about housing affordability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917733,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in terms of more or less rent control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921366,
    "dDurationMs": 5434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can have cities like New York\nor Amsterdam, where the housing market"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926800,
    "dDurationMs": 4666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is excessively regulated and they do not\nbuild enough public housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932166,
    "dDurationMs": 2967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the regulation itself\nis not necessarily the problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 935133,
    "dDurationMs": 2367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The building part is really the problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937500,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vienna\nfigured out through decades of experience"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941700,
    "dDurationMs": 1766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how to have a controlled market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943466,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet build more homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946466,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But given that most cities\ntoday are not inside crumbling empires"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950500,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as far as we know,\nor have not recently been bombed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954666,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think that for most cities,\nthe takeaway should be that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958833,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they should both encourage\nprivate construction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962100,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as build more high quality\npublic housing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966800,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is not just for the poorest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969700,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The takeaway should be\nthat they should do these things together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974266,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and doing them together\ncan solve the housing affordability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977333,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crisis,\nwhich is about building more homes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 980400,
    "dDurationMs": 1566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But yeah, that's my take."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981966,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me know what you guys think about\nthe Vienna model in the comments below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986666,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you want to know more\nabout the Vienna model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988766,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or about the role\nof social housing in general,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990666,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I highly recommend\nthat you check out the following three key"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 994566,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "articles from our advertising sponsor,\nThe Economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 998500,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
